    "accuracyGuardrails": "Show blood-cell and tumor evidence as parallel source comparisons. A plasma variant can originate outside tumor; matching one compartment or using a CHIP label does not resolve every source/function question.",
    "reasoning": "The blood-cell clone and solid tumor enter the plasma pool through parallel paths. A distinct comparison lists the same generic V in plasma and blood-cell DNA, with V not detected in sampled tumor material. This supports a blood-cell contribution without excluding every tumor contribution; assay limits, sampling and shared variants remain explicit. It does not equate a source clue with formal CHIP classification or a clinical risk forecast. The extension supplies the precise compartment comparison absent from the original flow.",
